   "failure_scenario": "Someone closes a factory PR on GitHub without merging it while the land queue has a pushed commit recorded, and then the daemon resumes. The queue correctly blocks and does not merge, but the reason it shows is \"cannot confirm current GitHub merge state\" rather than \"PR was closed\". The operator is pointed toward a GitHub or lookup problem instead of the real cause.",
   "reproduction": "unreproduced: not run; at head the resume guard sends every state other than OPEN or MERGED to the same throw, so the message for CLOSED follows directly from the quoted lines",
   "evidence": "Head src/land/queue.ts:336-341 (new in base..head): `if (entry.pushedSha) { const fresh = await this.mergeMetadata(entry.prUrl, signal); ... if (!fresh || fresh.url !== entry.prUrl || ![\"OPEN\", \"MERGED\"].includes(fresh.state)) throw new LandBlocked(\"cannot confirm current GitHub merge state\");`. A definite CLOSED observation with the matching URL takes the same branch as a missing, wrong-URL or malformed observation. The outcome is still safe: the entry blocks and no merge command runs. Only the reason text is wrong. Base had no such guard."
  },
  "B": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "Someone closes a pull request without merging while its landing entry awaits recovery. After restart, the queue correctly blocks it but reports uncertainty about GitHub instead of explaining that the pull request was closed, causing unnecessary investigation.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun \"$TMPDIR/f1-adjudication-56qi3l85/f1.ts\"",
    "output": "{\"freshState\":\"CLOSED\",\"matchingUrl\":true,\"matchingHead\":true,\"retainedSnapshot\":\"OPEN/SUCCESS\",\"error\":\"cannot confirm current GitHub merge state\",\"freshReads\":1,\"mergeCalls\":0}"
   },
   "evidence": "The throwaway script invokes HEAD's actual land method with an injected GitHub client returning CLOSED and matching URL/head; context and claim ownership are stubbed. HEAD checks `!fresh || fresh.url !== entry.prUrl || ![\"OPEN\", \"MERGED\"].includes(fresh.state)` and throws `LandBlocked(\"cannot confirm current GitHub merge state\")`. Thus a definite CLOSED observation receives the uncertainty diagnostic. Base has no corresponding fresh-observation recovery guard; this diagnostic branch was introduced by base..head. The later commit adds an earlier matching-URL/head CLOSED branch throwing `LandBlocked(\"PR was closed without merging\")` and extends the stale-snapshot regression test with that case."
  }
